{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And this land we took possession of at that time</b> — this land mentioned above, from the wadi Arnon to Mount Hermon, we took possession of at that time. <b>From Aroer, which is on the wadi Arnon</b> — this is not connected to the beginning of the verse but to its end, 'I gave to the Reubenites and to the Gadites'; however, regarding the matter of possession, it extended up to Mount Hermon. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 3:12). And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that it says: 'And this land that we took possession of at that time, from Aroer — I gave to the Reubenites and to the Gadites.' And similarly, 'and you shall make known to them the way they shall go in it' (Exodus 18:20), and so there are many such instances."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:44:36.066590934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}